170 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 519 0 R
/ActualText (New method for improving language generation by combining pre-trained language models with external memory sources. Introduces retrieval-augmented generation \(RAG\) models that merge a pre-trained sequence-to-sequence model with a dense vector index of Wikipedia accessed through a neural retriever.This approach helps overcome limitations in accessing and updating knowledge and leads to better performance on various knowledge-heavy tasks, setting new benchmarks in open-domain QA and producing more accurate and factual responses compared to traditional LLM.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
171 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 520 0 R
/ActualText (Gao, L., Ma, X., Lin, J. and Callan, J., 2022. Precise zero-shot dense retrieval without relevance labels. arXiv preprint arXiv:2212.10496.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
172 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 521 0 R
/ActualText (Hypothetical Document Embeddings \(HyDE\) to solves the problem of zero-shot dense retrieval when no relevance labels are available. HyDE involves generating a hypothetical document using an instruction-following language model, which captures relevance patterns but may contain inaccuracies. This document is then encoded into an embedding vector by an unsupervised contrastively learned encoder, which identifies similar real documents in the corpus. HyDE outperforms the state-of-the-art unsupervised dense retriever Contriever and shows strong performance comparable to fine-tuned retrievers across various tasks and languages.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
