195 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 537 0 R
/ActualText (FiD-Light adapts the Fusion-in-Decoder model for efficient retrieval-augmented text generation. It compresses encoded passage representations before decoding, reducing latency while maintaining effectiveness. The model incorporates source pointing capabilities to enable citation of relevant passages and improve provenance retrieval. Additionally, FiD-Light introduces a robust re-ranking approach using source pointers to mitigate distribution shifts between training and evaluation. These innovations enhance the model's efficiency, traceability, and adaptability in various text generation tasks.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
196 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 538 0 R
/ActualText (Wang, S., Khramtsova, E., Zhuang, S. and Zuccon, G., 2024, July. Feb4rag: Evaluating federated search in the context of retrieval augmented generation. In Proceedings of the 47th International ACM SIGIR Conference on Research and Development in Information Retrieval \(pp. 763-773\).)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
197 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 539 0 R
/ActualText (FeB4RAG introduces a novel federated search dataset for Retrieval Augmented Generation frameworks. It comprises 16 search engines built from BEIR datasets and advanced retrieval models, along with 790 conversational information requests. The dataset leverages Large Language Models to generate relevance judgments, which show high agreement with human annotations. FeB4RAG also provides insights into resource importance and query distribution across search engines, offering a valuable resource for developing and evaluating federated RAG systems.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
